🚽 Test case: #193 -- pointer-to-struct return types are now supported
🚽 (see struct_pointer_return.brainrot), but returning a BY-VALUE struct
🚽 from a pointer-returning function (`gang Point *f() { ... bussin p; }`
🚽 where p is a `gang Point`, not a pointer) is a type error: the return
🚽 value is not a pointer, so there is nothing to store into the pointer
🚽 destination.
gang Point {
    rizz x;
};

gang Point *get_ptr() {
    gang Point p;
    p.x = 5;
    bussin p;
}

skibidi main {
    gang Point *r = get_ptr();
    bussin 0;
}
